language packs
├── when checking a matching typescript file
│   └── it reports no findings
├── when checking a drifted typescript file
│   └── it reports the missing and extra test
├── when checking a playwright style file
│   └── it treats test describe as a block
├── when extracting parameterized typescript tests
│   ├── it reports supported forms and ignores unrelated each calls
│   └── it reports each through a test alias
├── when resolving typescript aliases
│   ├── it resolves direct conditional and transitive aliases
│   ├── it bounds a one hundred link chain
│   └── it ignores aliases outside module scope
├── when scaffolding from a tree
│   ├── it renders rust modules and test functions
│   └── it renders nested describe blocks
├── when scaffolding hostile spec text
│   └── it escapes quotes and format braces
├── when a scaffolded file is checked
│   └── it reports no findings for hostile titles
└── when a builtin pack has a wasm twin
    ├── it keeps queries and templates identical
    └── it keeps release metadata identical
